speechtext:
Mr. Speaker, I rise on a matter of urgent and pressing necessity under the provisions of Standing Order 43, the circumstances of which speak for themselves. I move, seconded by the hon. member for Sas-katoon-Biggar (Mr. Hnatyshyn):
That this House require that the Minister of Justice appear before a parliamentary committee of this House and show cause why he, as Attorney General, authorized and directed the laying of technical charges against Dr. Alexander Peter Treu, in connection with the protection of documents under the Official Secrets Act, when the government was aware, at the same time, that Dr. Treu was still receiving classified documents and contracts dealing with defence matters from NATO;
and that the Minister of Supply and Services should also appear and show cause for the basis on which his Director of Security, Mr. S. M. Jenkyns, the Canadian security liaison with NATO, is alleged to have cancelled Dr. Treu's security clearance and to have been involved in instigating the investigation leading to the trial and conviction of Dr. Treu, when he, Mr. Jenkyns, was either present or knew that Dr. Treu participated in confidential meetings and continued to receive NATO contracts and documents.
